					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-207431#post-2368292</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-207431/scp-887-log#post-2368292</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2015 22:56:27 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Thekillerax</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1832151</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>It's related in the sense that &quot;Does the black moon howl?&quot; is a phrase that's supposed to have some significance in the Foundation's higher echelons, either as a code phrase, memetic kill phrase or whatever. It was a lot more popular in the olden days, but now most Tales where it's been mentioned have been deleted. There are still a couple things around that reference it, including <a href="http://05command.wikidot.com|">the official staff site</a>, that one SCP (I think it was in the 200s) that was a girl trapped in a printer, and TroyL's series of Tales on the 001 proposals, although nowadays it's mainly just used as an Easter egg type thing.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-207431#post-2368275</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
